## Original Content
Tensions between Türkiye and Israel have intensified following Ankara's request for an Interpol Red Notice against Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, days after Israeli strikes on a Syrian airbase near the Turkish border.

## Summary
Tensions between Türkiye and Israel have escalated after Türkiye requested an Interpol Red Notice for Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. This follows Israeli strikes on a Syrian airbase near the Turkish border, heightening regional conflicts.

## Key Points
- Türkiye has sought an Interpol Red Notice against Benjamin Netanyahu.
- Israeli strikes targeted a Syrian airbase close to the Turkish border.
- Relations between Türkiye and Israel are deepening due to these events.
- The incident reflects broader geopolitical tensions involving Syria.


